WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.202
-You have a new album out
right now,

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.004
"Great Songs From Stage
And Screen."

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.906
I love that you did this.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.810
You know I'm a fan
of your singing, as well.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.145
Does this come from
your parents?

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:16.616
How did you get into
the crooning and the singing?

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:20.019
-It does, yeah.
It was something that my parents

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:24.290
always felt was a very important
part of childhood,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.560
allowing the brain to develop
properly

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.330
required the inclusion of music.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.932
-Would they have parties, or
would they just have records?

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.536
-Yeah, there were parties.
My dad played the guitar.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:40.439
A friend of my parents started
a church choir when I was a kid,

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:41.974
and believe it or not,
I was in it.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:43.542
-Wow.
-If you can picture me

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.379
in a church choir.
-I can't, I really can't.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.715
-But nonetheless. Yes.
-Wow.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:53.553
And are these songs inspired by
them, or just songs you like?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:58.290
-These are all just --
it's just a hodgepodge of songs

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:02.795
all from films or shows
that I just felt like,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:07.399
you know, had never really had
a proper arrangement

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:10.236
written for them
in a pop format.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.538
So it's a very light,
bubbly album.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:16.209
-It must be fun to do this
with the orchestra.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.378
I mean, it's a big production.
It sounds amazing.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:23.282
-Yeah, I love it.
I mean, it's my favorite part

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:26.019
of the film process
is the score,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:29.856
but, yeah, we recorded this
at Abbey Road.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.791
-No!
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:36.162
-You had to cross the street,
I'm assuming.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.597
-Cross the street?
Oh, yes, yes.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.400
From the other side
of the street.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.202
Oh, yeah. Oh, The Beatles,
-The Beatles. Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:48.741
You got to do that.
-I think it's the fourth

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.243
or fifth album
that we've done there.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.512
-Oh, really?
So you're used to this.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.780
What is it like inside?
I've never gone inside.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.250
-It's a cool place.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.186
And what's interesting about it
is there's carpeting,

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.821
there's wood paneling,
at least when I was there.

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:06.092
Structural elements that look
like, you know,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.460
if you were in someone's house,
you'd go,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.529
"It might be time to replace
this floor or this carpet.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.365
Looks like it's been there
forever, and it's just filthy."

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:16.703
-Yeah.
-But there's sort of a feeling

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.738
that, look, we don't know
what makes these acoustics

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.809
so magical, so we're not going
to mess with anything.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.177
I think part of it is
superstition,

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.212
and part of it is just
you really never know

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:31.784
what that X factor is, and so
best not to mess with it.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.053
-Did you get to the roof at all,
or no?

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.055
-No, I didn't go to the roof.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.991
-Is there something on the roof?
-That's the Beatles. Right?

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:42.328
Didn't they do it on the roof
of Abbey Road.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.663
-Oh, is that where they...

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:47.033
-Recorded "Let It Be."
-Yeah.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.435
And that's where they got
stopped by the police,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.003
and it was -- Yeah.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.238
Well, if you make another album,
I'll meet you out there.

00:02:53.238 --> 00:02:56.342
-Was it "Sgt. Pepper's" that
they just put a speaker

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.411
in a window and blasted it out
into the street,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.746
and that was how they
introduced it to the world?

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.649
-I mean, it's just --
-It may be apocryphal.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:06.785
I remember reading that story is
that they just opened a window,

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:08.321
here's the new record,

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.755
and people just stopped
and listened.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.258
-That must feel so cool
to record in Abbey Road.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.326
-It was fun. It was fun.
-I love the cover,

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:16.496
by the way, as well.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.999
With this type of music, I feel
like it is a solo mission.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.701
It's almost, you want it to look
lonely or something.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:27.740
But was it done pre-COVID
or pre-quarantine?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.410
-Yeah, there's some stuff
that we had to do back here

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.812
because obviously we couldn't
get back there,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:38.084
but most of it was done there
prior to all this mess.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.685
-Well, congrats on the album.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.754
As if you're not busy enough,

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.391
executive produced
"Cosmos: Possible Worlds."

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.926
Tell everyone about this season.

00:03:47.926 --> 00:03:51.230
-This season,
"Cosmos: Possible Worlds,"

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.799
Ann Druyan once again is back
as showrunner,

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.268
along with Brannon Braga.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.070
Neil deGrasse Tyson
obviously is back.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.140
And this is great. You know,
it's taken us a long while

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.109
to get this thing
back on the air.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:09.048
It's been a long wait for
audiences, and yet here it is.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:13.052
And, you know, we sort of feel
like at this point in time

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:18.558
There's nothing that feels more
necessary or relevant than --

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:22.461
than something that elevates
the enterprise of science,

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:25.030
I think. I think we can take
all we can get right now.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.300
So it's -- much like the
original, it's fun,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.536
it's colorful, it's lively,
it's surprising.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.738
I think people
are going to dig it.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.672
-I want to show a clip.
Here's a look at

00:04:33.672 --> 00:04:36.675
"Cosmos: Possible Worlds."
Check it out.

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:41.180
-The DNA double helix.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.750
Star stuff.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.253
Oxygen, carbon, nitrogen --

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.123
elements cooked in the hearts
of distant scars

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.692
combined with hydrogen
from the big bang

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:55.928
to become alive
on this little world.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:59.732
Through random changes,
mutations in the genes,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.668
some of which led to more
successful life forms,

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.938
what we call evolution
by natural selection,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.740
the ladder grew,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.011
adding more and more rungs.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.882
It took another three billion
years for life to evolve

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:19.218
the complexity of the plants
and animals that you could see

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.654
with the naked eye.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:26.225 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:29.361
-My thanks to Seth MacFarlane.
"Cosmos:Possible Worlds"

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:32.531
premiers September 22nd
at 8:00 p.m. on Fox,

00:05:32.531 --> 00:05:36.235
and check out "Great Songs From
Stage And Screen," out now.

